      "hints": [
        "Apply chain rule to differentiate $2(3-2x)^{-2} - x$.",
        "Differentiate again for $\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}$.",
        "Integrate using $\\int 2(3-2x)^{-2}\\,dx = \\frac{1}{3-2x}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $y = 2(3-2x)^{-2} - x$ using the chain rule on the first term:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2(-2)(3 - 2x)^{-3} \\times (-2) - 1 = 8(3 - 2x)^{-3} - 1 = \\frac{8}{(3 - 2x)^3} - 1$$",
        "Differentiate again to find the second derivative:\n$$\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = 8(-3)(3 - 2x)^{-4} \\times (-2) = 48(3 - 2x)^{-4} = \\frac{48}{(3 - 2x)^4}$$",
        "Integrate $y$ with respect to $x$ using the reverse chain rule:\n$$\\int y\\,dx = \\frac{2(3 - 2x)^{-1}}{(-1)(-2)} - \\frac{1}{2}x^2 + c = \\frac{1}{3 - 2x} - \\frac{1}{2}x^2 + c$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
